  "identifier": "gow-ragnarok-progression-playbook-2026",
  "headline": "God of War Ragnarok progression playbook: a detour checklist that keeps your upgrades on pace",
  "description": "A step-by-step route philosophy: where to detour, what to upgrade, and what to standardize so you do not hit level-gap walls while following the story.",
  "articleBody": "Goal: keep upgrades on pace while staying story-first. Ragnarok difficulty is heavily influenced by level gaps, so a consistent detour schedule prevents most \"sudden\" walls.\n\nA. Your repeatable routine (every time you enter a new area)\n1) find the shop\n2) unlock shortcuts and key traversal routes\n3) prioritize upgrade materials (weapons > armor > runics/relics)\n4) equip two short, reliable runics (landable > flashy)\n\nB. Detour windows (story breakpoints)\n- Missions 1–4: build fundamentals. Fix your defense style (parry-first or evade-first) and invest into it.\n- Missions 5–6 (Vanaheim): when the River Delta opens, assemble a midgame foundation set (status or stability).\n- Mission 9 onward: boss pressure rises. If you feel behind, upgrade first rather than forcing attempts.\n- After mission 13: Vanaheim opens further; it becomes an efficient upgrade-material farm window.\n- Before mission 17: use this as a clean breakpoint if you want to assemble endgame sets.\n\nC. Upgrade triggers (when to stop and rebuild)\n- if enemies feel \"above\" you, treat it as a level-gap problem and upgrade immediately\n- if your runics whiff or lock you in long animations, swap to shorter options\n- if multi-target fights break your camera, prioritize Blades control and companion stagger/status\n\nD. Postgame order\n1) collect materials to raise baseline levels\n2) attempt optional bosses with stability builds\n3) switch to burst builds once consistent\n\nE. Minimum fail-safe kit\n- fixed defense style\n- 2 short runics\n- companion for stagger/status\n- learn only 3 punish windows per boss\n\nPair this page with the chapter build timeline to make skill and gear decisions automatic.",
  "articleSection": "game-guide",
  "inLanguage": "hi",
